A||||7||2birds||Ram Powergrip clutch, anyone? Opinions wanted please.||||1||
Z||000000||2birds||07-27-2000||10:48 PM||||I'm considering using one, since Ram's OEM is occasionally slipping after only 35,000 miles.  It is Supposed to have 30% more holding power, and Kevlar on one side of the disk.  $270 from Summit, plus a two week wait.||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||07-28-2000||08:07 AM||||you'll probly be fine.. but if toss on a power adder (eg. Nitrous, Turbo, S/C) you'll probly have a problem. I had a RAM i got from the Fiero Store. and it was fine for a short time till the first time I hit the nitrous then all it was was slip and slow. get a hold of <A HREF="http://www.clutchnet.com" TARGET=_blank>www.clutchnet.com</A>  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Megafiero||07-28-2000||09:10 AM||||hey 1FST2M6  what kind of Ram clutch was it? Was it just the regualar,heavy duty, or racing?  I use the Ram racing clutch and have had no problems with it, and I have been using it for quite so time now.  2birds, if you want to go with a different brand though, check out the Centerforce, they do have one for the Fiero also.<P>Megafiero||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||07-28-2000||02:01 PM||||According to the fiero store it was the racing one.. i killed a Centerforce too... they refunded me the cost of the clutch! Centerforce are a great bunch of people. They just aren't made for nitrous shocks. (on our application) i'm sure with a turbo since the power doesn't come on so violently you should be ok.. same with S/C but i'm not sure. the soild disc 4 puck although a bit of a pain in traffic NEVER faild me.. 16 bottles of nitrous 15+ runs down the drag strip, few laps at Road Atlanta and back and for to work.. 6000miles and no problem.. where the others failed in the first 3 days... The CF and RAM required a breakin period which was adheared to 4-500miles city driving. the solid disc no breakin... plug and play. 1 hour after the car was back on the ground it was on the dyno being flogged with no ill effects. GT Bastard and Black GT are now the owners of these clutches. And i talk to Todd (Black GT) all the time and he loves it.. Jeff (Gt Bastard) however seems to tolerate it...  ok.. lost the subject... The RAM clutch pack will be fine as long as your running a pretty stock setup... or as long as you show a little discretion with your power adders. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||PJ||07-28-2000||08:15 PM||||I'm on my second Ram performance clutch, I think they call it Powergrip, and its an improvement on the organic disks. Its a two sided kevlar disk with a stock pressure plate and throwout bearing. Even though I beat the hell out of it road racing the car, the disk holds up well with a normally aspirated 2.8L. The recent replacement I had to perform was because of a failed pressure plate. Two of the springs wore through and broke off where they contact the throwout bearing, but I don't think this would be an issue in a purely street car. Its a good, reliable performance upgrade without the drivability problems associated with high performance clutchs.<P>PJ<BR>ITA #66 Black  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||lowCG||07-29-2000||09:21 AM||||Probably not much help,but I just installed a Ram clutch,purchased from West coast Fiero($270)that has a kevlar lining on both sides of the disc,is very driveable,haven't thrashed on it yet though.||||reg||1
Z||000006||2birds||07-29-2000||11:19 PM||||I read on here a while back that the Centerforce for Fieros was basically an orange spray painted LUK pressure plate (same as OEM and my Ram setup), without the weights that help the regular Centerforce pressure plates increase their grip with RPM.  Something about there isn't enough room in the getrag bellhousing for them.  For almost 3 and a half blls, I don't think so...<BR>Thanks for the clutchnet link.  I'll check it out.||||reg||1
Z||000007||1FST2M6||07-31-2000||08:28 AM||||2birds is right... the RAM is actually a Borg&Beck unit. with a little different lining. thats why CF refunded me the $260 for the Dual Friction that failed in 3 days.. RAm swears it was user error and improper breakin.  <A HREF="http://www.clutchnet.com" TARGET=_blank>www.clutchnet.com</A>   their stuff ROCKS! ||||reg||1
